hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20892","Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, when you swear an oath, then see another better than it, then do what is better and expiate your oath."
"20893","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Hayyan ibn Umayr, Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah narrated to us, he said: While I was shooting my arrows during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), by Allah, the sun eclipsed, so I threw them aside and hastened to see what happened to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the sun's eclipse, and behold he was raising his hands, glorifying Allah, mighty and majestic, praising, declaring His oneness, magnifying Him, and supplicating, and he remained so until the sun cleared, then he recited two surahs and prayed two rak'ahs."
"20894","Isma'il narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it upon asking, you will be left to it, and if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it, and when you swear an oath, then see another better than it, then do what is better and expiate your oath."
"20895","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from Abu Labid, he said: We campaigned with Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah to Kabul, and the people took sheep and plundered them, so Abd al-Rahman ordered a caller to call: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever plunders plunder is not of us, so return these sheep, so they returned them, and he divided them equally."
"20896","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting, and most of my knowledge is that I heard it from him, Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Nasih ibn al-Ala, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, that he passed by Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah while he was at the river of Umm Abdullah, water flowing, with his youths and freedmen, so Ammar said to him: O Abu Sa'id, the Friday prayer, so Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: When it is a rainy day, let one of you pray in his lodging."
"20897","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Nasih ibn al-Ala Abu al-Ala narrated to us, Ammar ibn Abi Ammar narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I heard al-Qawariri say: I used to pass by Nasih and he would narrate to me, and when I asked him for more he said: I have nothing but this, and he was blind."
"20898","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah al-Qurashi narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it upon asking, you will be entrusted to it, and if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it, and when you swear an oath, then see another better than it, then do what is better and expiate your oath."
"20899","Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Simak ibn Atiyyah and Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"20900","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not swear by your fathers, nor by the taghuts. And Yazid said: And the taghut."
"20901","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Ibn Awn from al-Hasan from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah who said: He mentioned the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: He said: Do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it without asking you will be helped in it, and if you are given it through asking you will be entrusted to it, and if you swear an oath and see another better than it, then do what is better and make expiation for your oath."
"20902","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us from Yala ibn Hakim from Abu Labid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever plunders plunder is not from us."
"20903","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from al-Hasan from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said to him: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it through asking you will be entrusted to it, and if you are given it without asking you will be helped in it, and if you swear an oath and see another better than it, then make expiation for your oath and do what is better."
"20904","Aswad ibn Amir and Affan narrated to us, they said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it through asking you will be entrusted to it, and if you are given it without asking you will be helped in it, and if you swear an oath and see another better than it, then make expiation for your oath and do what is better. My father said: Affan and Aswad agreed in their hadith, they said: So make expiation for your oath then do what is better. And Abu al-Ashhab said from al-Hasan in this hadith: So he began with the expiation."
"20905","Husayn narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us from al-Hasan, Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah al-Qurashi narrated to us while we were in Kabul, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, then he mentioned the hadith."
"20906","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Harun ibn Maruf, Damrah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Shawdhab narrated to us from Abdullah ibn al-Qasim from Kathir, freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah who said: Uthman ibn Affan came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a thousand dinars in his garment when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was equipping the army of hardship. He said: He poured it into the lap of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began turning it over with his hand and saying: No harm will befall Ibn Affan whatever he does after today, repeating it many times."
"20907","Affan narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Yala ibn Hakim narrated to us from Abu Labid who said: We campaigned with Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah to Kabul. He said: The people got booty and plundered it, so Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah ordered a caller to call out, so he called out, the people gathered, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever plunders is not from us. Return them, so they returned them, and he divided it among them equally."
